-- int-tests-repairs: what changed after the independent testing, run through the headlines.  Two groups were repaired on 2026-10-27: G2 (the facts of Article 6(1)(i) gained the object of improving the conditions of life; a body that is
-- not an entity cannot meet the charity test, Article 5(1); fork F2.13: the Commissioner's staff exercising a function under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)) and G7 (a Part's stages come from every Article it held, so Part 9 is in force from
-- 1 January 2019 on reading A of F7.9; Articles 21 and 23 reach an entity within Article 2(1) only).  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run:
--   Article 6(1)(i): "the provision of recreational facilities, or the organisation of recreational activities, with the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom the facilities or activities are primarily
--   intended"; Article 6(2)(d): paragraph (1)(i) "applies only in relation to recreational facilities or activities that are (i) primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability,
--   financial hardship or other disadvantage, or (ii) available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large";
--   Article 5(1): "An entity meets the charity test if ..."; Article 2(1)(i): an unincorporated body or association of persons "other than a partnership" (so a partnership is within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1), unless (j));
--   Article 7(3)(b) and 7(1): the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court must not treat an entity that benefits only identified natural persons as providing public benefit; Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3): functions of the Commissioner may
--   be exercised by members of the Commissioner's staff, except the decisions under Articles 11, 15(3) and 16 (src:796);
--   the Table of Legislation History (src:874-880) and R&O.17/2018 Article 2: the original Article 41 (spent) and Part 6 came into force on 1 January 2019, the Parts 1 to 3, Article 32 and Articles 38 to 44 (original) on 21 November 2014, the
--   Parts 4, 5, 7, Articles 33 to 37 on 1 May 2018;
--   Article 21(3), 21(5): "A Jersey entity that is not a registered charity ..." and "An entity that is not a registered charity and is neither ...": they name an entity.

§ `Integration layer -- the repairs`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with F2.13 read as B` MEANS `Int fx the readings with the reading of Articles 3 to 7` fleet `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.13 read as B`
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with F7.9 read as B` MEANS `Int fx the readings with the reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` fleet `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.9`

GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision to register` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision to refuse` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner refuses`

-- The applicant of these scenarios: a body with a given name, kind and purposes, a director who lives in Jersey, a registered office in Jersey, a name with no objection, a complete application, no bar.
GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The applicant's name
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts G1 reads about the body
      purposes IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` @desc The purposes with the facts Article 6 reads
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`an applicant body called` name `of the kind` facts `with the purposes` purposes MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH name IS name, standing IS `an applicant for registration`, purposes IS purposes, facts IS facts, model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS (LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun"))

GIVEN body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The applicant
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit` @desc The determination of public benefit
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`an application by` body `with the determination` determination MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS body
        `charity test facts` IS `Int fx the charity test facts with` determination
        application IS `Int fx a complete application lodged on` (YMD 2026 6 1)
        findings IS `Int fx clear findings`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS `Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
        `opinion on the name` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` (body's name)
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`the Commissioner's determination` MEANS `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`

GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a staff determination that finds public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified persons` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `a member of the Commissioner's staff`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS TRUE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

§§ `R1: a recreational purpose -- Article 6(1)(i) and 6(2)(d) -- with and without the object of improving the conditions of life`

-- A company whose only purpose is to run a sports hall open to the public.  6(2)(d)(ii) is met (available to the public at large).
GIVEN atLarge IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Whether the facilities are available to members of the public at large
      need IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Whether the facilities are primarily intended for persons in need
      object IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Whether the facilities have the object of improving the conditions of life
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`a recreational purpose` atLarge need object MEANS
    `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` WITH purpose IS (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to run a sports hall open to the public" `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`), facts IS (`Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
            `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
            `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
            `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
            `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
            `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS need
            `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS atLarge
            `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
            `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
            `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING
            `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS object)

GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` @desc The only purpose
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application of a sports company with the purpose` purpose MEANS
    `an application by` (`an applicant body called` "Gorey Sports Limited" `of the kind` (`Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))) `with the purposes` (LIST purpose)) `with the determination` `the Commissioner's determination`

-- The object is stated true: the purpose is charitable, so the test is met and the Commissioner must register.
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE))))'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE))))'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE))))'s `the application may be granted`
-- The object is stated false: the purpose is not charitable (6(1)(i)); the only purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary, so the test fails and the Commissioner must refuse.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE))))'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE))))'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
-- The object is not stated and 6(2)(d) is met: the Law's condition cannot be decided, and the encoding refuses by name (G2: the refusal is the intended signal that the new field is missing).
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING)))'s `the entity meets the charity test` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING)))'s duty BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life"
-- The object is not stated but 6(2)(d) is not met on either alternative (not for persons in need, not available to the public at large): head (i) does not apply whatever the object is, so the purpose is not charitable and the answer is
-- a refusal to register, not a refusal to answer.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING)))'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING)))'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
-- 6(2)(d)(i): a hall primarily for persons in need, with the object stated, also qualifies although it is not open to the public at large.
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE))))'s `the entity meets the charity test`

§§ `R2: a non-entity applicant -- a partnership -- Article 2(1)(i) and Article 5(1)`

-- An unincorporated partnership governed by the law of Jersey is "other than a partnership" excluded from 2(1)(i) and is within no other sub-paragraph, so it is not an entity; "An entity meets the charity test if ..." (5(1)), so it cannot.
-- Its purpose is the same charitable purpose as the school company's.
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`a partnership applying` MEANS
    `an applicant body called` "Gorey Tutors" `of the kind` (`Int fx a body with` (LIST `it is an unincorporated body`, `it is a partnership`, `its relationship is governed by the law of Jersey`) EMPTY) `with the purposes` (LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`)))
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application of a partnership` MEANS `an application by` `a partnership applying` `with the determination` `the Commissioner's determination`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of a partnership`)'s entity's `kinds of entity` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of a partnership`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of a partnership`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of a partnership`)'s decision EQUALS JUST `the decision to refuse`
-- The same purposes in a company are accepted (A1), so it is the want of an entity that decides.
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the application of a sports company with the purpose` (`a recreational purpose` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE))))'s entity's `kinds of entity` EQUALS LIST `a company`

§§ `R3: a determination made by a member of the Commissioner's staff -- Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) -- both readings of F2.13`

-- A member of the Commissioner's staff finds public benefit for a company that benefits only identified natural persons.  Article 7(3)(b) forbids "the Commissioner" (7(1): the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court) to treat such an
-- entity as providing public benefit.  Reading taken (A): a function exercised on the Commissioner's behalf is the Commissioner's function, so the staff are bound, the finding does not make the entity one that provides public benefit
-- and the test fails.  Reading B: only the persons 7(1) names are bound, the finding stands and the test is met.  (The decision under Article 11 whether to register is itself reserved from staff, Schedule 1 4(3)(a); only the
-- determination of public benefit is made by staff here.)
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application with a staff determination` MEANS `an application by` (`an applicant body called` "Gorey Schools Limited" `of the kind` (`Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))) `with the purposes` (LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`)))) `with the determination` `a staff determination that finds public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified persons`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a staff determination`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a staff determination`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` `the readings with F2.13 read as B` (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a staff determination`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` `the readings with F2.13 read as B` (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a staff determination`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
-- The same finding made by the Commissioner is not permitted on either reading (7(1) names the Commissioner), so the test fails on both.
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`the Commissioner's determination of the same finding` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS TRUE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application with the Commissioner's determination of the same finding` MEANS `an application by` (`an applicant body called` "Gorey Schools Limited" `of the kind` (`Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))) `with the purposes` (LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`)))) `with the determination` `the Commissioner's determination of the same finding`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with the Commissioner's determination of the same finding`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` `the readings with F2.13 read as B` (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with the Commissioner's determination of the same finding`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`

§§ `R4: Part 9 and the original Article 41 -- headline (e) -- the units in force on 2018-04-30, 2018-06-01 and 2019-01-01`

-- The Parts, from the Table of Legislation History (src:874-880) and R&O.17/2018: Parts 1 to 3 from 21 November 2014; Parts 4, 5 and 7 from 1 May 2018; Part 6 from 1 January 2019.  Part 8 has two stages (Article 32, 21 November 2014; Articles 33 to 36,
-- 1 May 2018).  Part 9 has three: Articles 38 to 43 (21 November 2014), Article 37 (1 May 2018) and the original Article 41 (the remainder, 1 January 2019).  Reading taken (A of F7.9): a Part is in force when all its Articles are.
-- The other reading (B): when any of its Articles is.
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 5 1))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 6 1))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 12 31))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2019 1 1))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` `the readings with F7.9 read as B` (YMD 2018 4 30))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 8, 9
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` `the readings with F7.9 read as B` (YMD 2018 6 1))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` `the readings with F7.9 read as B` (YMD 2019 1 1))'s `Parts in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9
-- The Articles as now numbered: stage 1 is 1 to 7, 32 and 38 to 43 (14 Articles); stage 2 adds 8 to 20, 26 to 31 and 33 to 37 (24, so 38); stage 3 adds 21 to 25 (so 43).  Present Article 41 (the original 42) is in force from 2014, whatever Part 9 is.
#ASSERT count ((`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30))'s `Articles in force`) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT count ((`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 6 1))'s `Articles in force`) EQUALS 38
#ASSERT count ((`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2019 1 1))'s `Articles in force`) EQUALS 43
#ASSERT elem 41 ((`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30))'s `Articles in force`)
#ASSERT NOT elem 21 ((`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 6 1))'s `Articles in force`)
#ASSERT elem 37 ((`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 6 1))'s `Articles in force`)
#ASSERT NOT elem 37 ((`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30))'s `Articles in force`)
#ASSERT (`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30))'s `Schedules in force` EQUALS LIST 1, 2

§§ `R5: a non-entity says it is a charity -- headline (d) -- Articles 21 and 23 name an entity`

GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`a level 3 fine and no imprisonment` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING, fine IS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3
GIVEN thebody IS A `Body in the case` @desc The body that says it is a charity
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the body calls itself a charity` thebody MEANS
    `a statement about an entity` WITH
        body IS thebody
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `Int fx the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        statement IS `Int fx a statement by the entity itself saying` `that it is a “charity”`
GIVEN thebody IS A `Body in the case` @desc The body
GIVETH AN `Offence case`
`the offence case of` thebody MEANS `Offence case` WITH act IS `the body calls itself a charity` thebody, officer IS NOTHING

GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`a partnership not on the register` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH name IS "Gorey Tutors", standing IS `not on the register`, purposes IS (LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`))), facts IS `Int fx a body with` (LIST `it is an unincorporated body`, `it is a partnership`, `its relationship is governed by the law of Jersey`) EMPTY, model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS (LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun"))
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`an NPO body corporate not on the register` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH name IS "Les Amis du Jardin", standing IS `not on the register`, purposes IS (LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`))), facts IS `Int fx an NPO body corporate`, model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS (LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "M. Du Feu"))
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`a Jersey company not on the register` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH name IS "Les Pommiers Limited", standing IS `not on the register`, purposes IS (LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to relieve poverty in Jersey" `the prevention or relief of poverty`))), facts IS `Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "P. Gallichan")), model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS (LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "P. Gallichan"))

-- A partnership is no entity: no prohibition of 21 binds it, so there is no offence and no penalty (it would be one for a Jersey company, D1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the offence case of` `a partnership not on the register`))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the offence case of` `a partnership not on the register`))'s penalties EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the offence case of` `a Jersey company not on the register`))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the offence case of` `a Jersey company not on the register`))'s penalties EQUALS LIST `a level 3 fine and no imprisonment`
-- An NPO body corporate established in Jersey is an entity only from 16 October 2025 (sub-paragraph (ba), R&O.56/2025): on 15 October 2025 it is none, so no offence; on 16 October 2025 it is a Jersey entity that is not a registered
-- charity and the strict offence of 21(3) is made out (level 3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2025 10 15) (`the offence case of` `an NPO body corporate not on the register`))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2025 10 16) (`the offence case of` `an NPO body corporate not on the register`))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2025 10 16) (`the offence case of` `an NPO body corporate not on the register`))'s penalties EQUALS LIST `a level 3 fine and no imprisonment`

§§ `R6: headline (a) is gated by commencement -- 30 April 2018 against 1 May 2018`

-- Group G4's own duty (Article 11(4)) takes no day, by design (IP4: no group gates itself); the headline does.  Part 4 came into force on 1 May 2018, so on 30 April 2018 the first Article in the list that is not in force is Article 8.
-- On 1 May 2018 the Articles are in force, and the headline refuses for the other reason that applies to every day before 1 January 2019: no text of the Law before that day is among the sources.
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application of the school company` MEANS `an application by` (`an applicant body called` "Gorey Schools Limited" `of the kind` (`Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))) `with the purposes` (LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`)))) `with the determination` `the Commissioner's determination`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the school company`)'s `the application may be granted`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30) `the application of the school company`) BECAUSE "Article 8 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2018 5 1) `the application of the school company`) BECAUSE "no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources"
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2019 1 1) `the application of the school company`)'s `the application may be granted`
